I would suggest  the place structure

na'orcu'o: x1 is random with a normal distribution, and has mean x2, and SD x3

I believe that this order reflects the frequency of use of the places, and 
I don't see the value of a "conditions" place. The conditions on x1 can be 
expressed within the statement of x1. There is only one normal 
distribution, and it is specified entirely by its mean and SD.


           

